# GitHub Workflow

## Issues

Every piece of meaningful work has a GitHub issue at
**https://github.com/r4kh4t/antarctica-am-draft/issues**

### When to open an issue

Open one before starting any `feat`, `fix`, or `refactor` work:

```bash
# Feature
gh issue create --title "feat: <short description>" --label "feature" \
  --milestone "v1.5.0 — Next"

# Bug
gh issue create --title "fix: <short description>" --label "bug" \
  --milestone "v1.5.0 — Next"
```

### Labels

| Label | Use |
|---|---|
| `feature` | New feature or enhancement |
| `bug` | Something broken or incorrect |
| `refactor` | Code restructure, no behaviour change |
| `infrastructure` | CI/CD, tooling, hooks, devex |
| `documentation` | Docs, changelog, comments |

### Milestones

| Milestone | Status | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `v0.8.0 — Initial Delivery` | closed | All delivered take-home features |
| `v0.9.0 — Refinement` | closed | Earlier post-submission improvements (complete) |
| `v1.5.0 — Next` | open | Current backlog — new issues default here |

## Commit Message Linkage

For `feat`, `fix`, and `refactor` commits, include the issue number:

```
feat(llm): add streaming support (#14)
fix(table): correct sort direction on reload (#15)
```

The `commit-msg` Husky hook shows an advisory warning if no `#N` is found
in a `feat`/`fix`/`refactor` commit. It does not block — linking is
strongly recommended but not hard-enforced.

## PR Template

Every PR uses `.github/pull_request_template.md`, which requires:
- `Closes #N` in the description (auto-closes the issue on merge)
- CHANGELOG.md and package.json version updated
- Tests, lint, build passing

## Project Board

Issues are tracked on the GitHub Project board.
To create it (requires `project` scope):

```bash
bash scripts/create-project-board.sh
```

To grant the scope first:

```bash
gh auth refresh -h github.com -s project
```
